            "id": "zh-p04-teach-contrast",
            "type": "explain",
            "heading": "Choose by context",
            "explanation": "A Chinese character can appear in several words with different functions. 你 refers to one person; 你们 is plural. 你好 is a greeting and is not translated by adding the two character glosses. 好吃 means that food tastes good, not a way of saying hello. Pinyin carries tone marks: nǐ is third tone and hǎo is third tone in citation form. This text-only preview does not measure connected-speech tone sandhi or spoken accuracy.",
